Expose Darwin 26 (iPadOS 27.0.1 / 24A446) security.mac.lockdown_mode_state_public sysctl.

In 24A446, libsystem_darwin's os_lockdown_mode_enabled_block_invoke (called by /sbin/launchd
immediately after 'Early boot complete. Continuing system boot.') queries
security.mac.lockdown_mode_state_public and aborts (SIGABRT, namespace 2 subcode 0x6) if
sysctlbyname returns ENOENT. Verified verbatim against 24A446 Apple kernelcache (0xa0d05).

diff --git a/bsd/kern/lockdown_mode.c b/bsd/kern/lockdown_mode.c
--- a/bsd/kern/lockdown_mode.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/lockdown_mode.c
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
 
 SYSCTL_DECL(_security_mac);
 SYSCTL_INT(_security_mac, OID_AUTO, lockdown_mode_state, CTLFLAG_RD | CTLFLAG_LOCKED, &lockdown_mode_state, 0, "Lockdown Mode state");
+SYSCTL_INT(_security_mac, OID_AUTO, lockdown_mode_state_public, CTLFLAG_RD | CTLFLAG_LOCKED, &lockdown_mode_state, 0, "Lockdown Mode state (public)");
 
 __startup_func
 void
